  "id": "DrugBank_DB00663 - MONDO_15758",
  "verbalization": "Flumethasone appears to be a potential candidate for repurposing in the treatment of Primary Cutaneous T-cell Lymphoma (PCTCL) based on its association with Prednicarbate, a corticosteroid with known anti-inflammatory and immunosuppressive properties. The evidence suggests that Flumethasone, through its indication for Lichen Disease, Granuloma Annulare, and Chronic Cutaneous Lupus Erythematosus, may exert a therapeutic effect via a shared mechanism with Prednicarbate, which is known to target the immune system and inhibit tumor growth. The overlapping pathways indicate a possible role for corticosteroids in modulating immune responses and suppressing pathological inflammation, which could be relevant in the treatment of PCTCL. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Flumethasone to be considered for repurposing in this context, supported by a convergent evidence base linking it to a class of drugs with established therapeutic effects on immune-mediated disorders.",
